00:03:53.102 --> 00:03:58.922
states. Simon Willison used Claude code to build beep locator, a multi-device

00:03:58.922 --> 00:04:04.042
acoustic triangulation system that listens across laptops, iPads, and phones for an

00:04:04.042 --> 00:04:06.102
unknown beep inside a room of boxes.

00:04:06.682 --> 00:04:10.702
It keeps 60-second audio buffers, lines the clips up with chirps,

00:04:11.022 --> 00:04:13.422
and shows likely source spots on a shared map.

00:04:14.022 --> 00:04:16.522
The source was an aging carbon monoxide detector.

00:04:17.502 --> 00:04:19.142
A machine learning sub-reddit thread

00:04:19.142 --> 00:04:22.142
